ert ratings, or market prices are available yet, so the outlook rests on the state's underlying partisan balance.\n\nRecent headlines center on down-ballot contests, including competitive primaries and a Democratic push to redraw congressional maps, but none of that directly alters the presidential picture. A popular Democratic governor seeking re-election could add modest coattails, while the national climate remains the main unknown. The state's fundamentals point to a comfortable but not guaranteed Democratic win, with room for a strong Republican environment to narrow the margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9506, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9102, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9258, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9136, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9144, "margin": 15.0}]}